n\\\": \\\"NodeNext\\\",\\n    \\\"lib\\\": [\\\"ES2022\\\"],\\n    \\\"outDir\\\": \\\"dist\\\",\\n    \\\"rootDir\\\": \\\"src\\\",\\n    \\\"strict\\\": true,\\n    \\\"noUncheckedIndexedAccess\\\": true,\\n    \\\"exactOptionalPropertyTypes\\\": true,\\n    \\\"declaration\\\": true,\\n    \\\"sourceMap\\\": true,\\n    \\\"skipLibCheck\\\": true\\n  },\\n  \\\"include\\\": [\\\"src/**/*\\\"]\\n}\\n\"}}","type":"input_text"},{"text":"{\"i\":2,\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"d30766\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000004208,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1679,\"output\":\"README.md:13:pre-push hook and fetch refspec (or explicitly, via `cledger sync`).\\nREADME.md:90:cledger records sync            # explicit fetch/merge/push of the ledger ref\\nREADME.md:91:cledger records reanchor        # what did the remote squash away? (--apply to map it)\\nREADME.md:109:  `cledger records sync --all` pushes the whole ledger.\\nREADME.md:116:  marked block from `.git/hooks/pre-push`. `cledger records sync` always works\\nREADME.md:140:  the change matches two commits, nothing is guessed. `cledger re-anchor`\\nREADME.md:144:  `cledger re-anchor OLD_REV... --onto NEW_REV` command for a human to confirm.\\nREADME.md:146:  commits are garbage collected. `cledger records reanchor` keeps the shared\\nREADME.md:294:**Sync-time scan** (default on, tiered): Before any push, scans only new events with medium/high-precision rules (capture ruleset re-run, keyword assignments like `password=`, URL credentials). Findings abort the ledger push, but the default output contains only aggregate counts and safe next-step guidance — no fingerprints or event coordinates. A human can deliberately request the coordinate-only report with `cledger records sync --report` (or `cledger scan --report` for the standalone scan). That report prints event id, rule, JSON path + offset, and fingerprint, but never a character of the flagged text or its surroundings. It is **grouped by fingerprint**: the same span recurring across an event's `content` and `raw` mirrors, or across every edit of one file, is one decision, and the report's size tracks decisions rather than match sites (this repo's own dogfood backlog was 153 sites that collapse to 11 spans). Coding agents should not request the report: even contentless credential-shaped coordinates can feed back into captured work. Readable content lives behind `cledger records review` (interactive, one screen per span) and `cledger records inspect --output FILE` (writes a `0600` file); both refuse to run inside a coding-agent session. The pre-push hook always uses concise output; a finding holds back only the ledger and lets your code push proceed unless `{\\\"transport\\\": {\\\"strict\\\": true}}`.\\nREADME.md:297:- Remediation paths: `cledger records review` (walk every outstanding span), `cledger records redact EVENT_ID --pattern REGEX` (real secrets), `cledger records allow FINGERPRINT` (false positives), `cledger records sync --no-scan` (human-only push bypass). `--paranoid` adds entropy-based detection to sync; review and inspect use `--tier paranoid`.\\nREADME.md:300:**Allowlist tiers**: a false positive is usually a property of the *text* (a fixture, a doc example), not of the repo it was captured in — the same span gets re-flagged in the next repo that quotes the same doc. `cledger records allow FINGERPRINT` records it for this repo (`.git/conversation-ledger/allowlist.json`); add `--global` for every repo on this machine (`~/.config/cledger/allowlist.json`); and a repo can commit shared entries in `.cledger.json` as `{\\\"scan\\\": {\\\"allowFingerprints\\\": [\\\"...\\\"]}}` so clones and teammates inherit them. All three union at scan time. Fingerprints are truncated `sha256` of a span a human judged *not* to be a secret, so committing them discloses nothing.\\nREADME.md:304:The canonical shared maintenance interface is `cledger records <command>`.\\nREADME.md:305:The original top-level `cledger sync`, `review`, `inspect`, `redact`, `allow`,\\nREADME.md:308:top-level `cledger transport-push`; `cledger records transport-push` is also\\nREADME.md:311:| Command after `cledger records` | Purpose |\\nREADME.md:315:| `inspect --output FILE [--tier standard\\\\|paranoid] [--context N] [--reveal]` | Write finding context to a private file. Human only; `--overwrite` permits replacing a file. |\\nREADME.md:321:`cledger records --help` prints the full command syntax. Exit status is `0`\\nREADME.md:333:| `cledger sync [--remote R] [--push\\\\|--fetch] [--all\\\\|--rev R] [--no-scan] [--paranoid] [--report]` | Choose a remote and a particular branch or commit for transport. |\\nREADME.md:335:| `cledger inspect EVENT_ID [--context N] [--reveal] [--stdout]` | Inspect one event, including allowed findings, in a private temporary file by default. Human only. |\\nREADME.md:338:| `cledger re-anchor [--target R] [--apply] [--no-forge]` | Show evidence-ranked candidates and a suggested manual command. |\\nREADME.md:339:| `cledger re-anchor OLD_REV... --onto REV` | Confirm an inexact mapping. Human only. |\\nREADME.md:342:The original `inspect --force` spelling remains accepted for compatibility,\\nREADME.md:362:`cledger records redact EVENT_ID (--pattern REGEX | --all) [--reason TEXT]`\\nREADME.md:613:  fixes. cledger records the work of building cledger, so its own state,\\nREADME.md:625:  `cledger sync`, and the pre-push gate now print only aggregate counts and\\nREADME.md:641:  push learns the granularity storage already had. `cledger sync` scopes to\\nREADME.md:642:  the current branch by default, `--rev` scopes elsewhere, `--all` restores\\nREADME.md:698:  the CLI at all. `cledger export` gains `--all` alongside `--rev`, matching\\nREADME.md:707:  its branch is not checked out), `cledger inspect` (an event id is a global\\nREADME.md:711:  *Consequence worth knowing:* after a `cledger records sync --fetch-only`, conversations\\nREADME.md:821:  the `cledger re-anchor` command for dry runs and manual assertions. The\\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:13:\\\"Transport\\\"); `cledger sync` remains the explicit path and the fallback when\\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:328:- `cledger re-anchor` is the explicit path: dry-run by default, `--apply`,\\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:360:  ref is never force-overwritten. `cledger sync`'s fetch phase uses the\\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:363:  (config), or delete the marked hook block. `cledger sync` stays available\\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:472:  Readable output moved to `cledger inspect <event-id>`, which renders wide\\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:474:  match unless `--reveal`, writes to a mode-0600 file outside the repo rather\\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:476:  via the harnesses' own env markers; `--force` overrides). That last guard is\\ndocs/WIP_TECHNICAL_DESIGN.md:489:  agent-session refusal as inspect, no `--force`, plus a hard TTY\\naf81962 Merge pull request #24 from evintunador/fix/restore-maintenance-commands\\nfd47011 Restore cledger maintenance command behavior\\na741de8 Export cledger Ledger factory for downstream records CLIs (#23)\\nbe5f2b9 Merge pull request #22 from evintunador/feat/records-dispatcher\\n453efcd Add canonical records commands via annals dispatcher\\na6821c7 Make scan findings concise by default (#21)\\n473ad0f docs: describe hashed known-secret storage (#20)\\n76f1fa1 Add explicit Claude Code project backfill (#19)\\n\"}}","type":"input_text"}],"type":"custom_tool_call_output"},"timestamp":"2026-09-25T13:09:59.660Z","type":"response_item"},"format":"codex-rollout-jsonl/2"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-25T13:10:48.104Z","schema":"annals/v1","stream":{"id":"codex:01a0d65d-0c06-7f41-ba99-97400cdf5b6d","seq":803}}
